{
  "slug": "zforge",
  "name": "Zforge",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Standardized GitHub development workflow skills.\n\nType a slash command, get a disciplined workflow. TDD, branch isolation, PR review, quality checklist — every time, no exceptions.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **16 skills** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (16): `add-feat` (Add a new feature with design, TDD, and PR workflow), `audit` (Audit a codebase for security vulnerabilities, code quality issues, and architecture concerns), `autopilot` (Use when the user says \"autopilot\", \"auto mode\", \"替我回答\", or \"自动回答\"), `blog` (Write personal blog posts with the rhythm, structure, and voice of top-tier essayists (Paul Graham, Dan Luu, Henrik…), `fix-bug` (Fix a bug with systematic debugging, TDD, and PR workflow), `git-release` (Create a git release — tag, push, and create GitHub release), `hotfix` (Emergency fix — minimal change, fast PR, no design overhead), `init-project` (Initialize a new project — repo, structure, CI, and first commit), and 8 more\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install zforge@claude-community` from `zhengxuyu/zforge`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
